From: meta-st-odyssey <build@local>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 00:35:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: stm32mp157c-odyssey: drop broken eth assigned-clocks

ethck_k (what "&rcc ETHCK_K" refers to) is a plain gate clock with
exactly one hardcoded parent name, "ck_ker_eth" - it has no mux of
its own (see clk-stm32mp1.c: "Particulary Kernel Clocks (no mux or
no gate)"). The actual PLL3_Q/PLL4_P mux lives one level up, in an
unnamed (NO_ID, not DT-addressable) composite clock.

So this board's

    assigned-clocks = <&rcc ETHCK_K>, <&rcc PLL4_P>;
    assigned-clock-parents = <&rcc PLL4_P>;
    assigned-clock-rates = <125000000>;

can never succeed: the kernel's of_clk_set_defaults() calls
clk_set_parent(ethck_k, pll4_p), the clk core looks for pll4_p in
ethck_k's own parent array (which contains only "ck_ker_eth"), finds
no match, and clk_fetch_parent_index() returns -EINVAL - logged every
boot as "clk: failed to reparent ethck_k to pll4_p: -22". This is a
plain clk-core topology mismatch, unrelated to OP-TEE/SCMI/ETZPC or
secure boot in any way, and cannot ever work as written, on any
kernel with this driver, on any board.

It's also unnecessary: ck_ker_eth's mux already defaults to PLL4_P
via the (still present) st,eth-clk-sel + OP-TEE/TF-A's static
CLK_ETH_PLL4P selection (see the tf-a-stm32mp and optee-os-stm32mp
bbappends in this same layer, which set PLL4 to the correct 750MHz
VCO for this board's KSZ9031RN). Confirmed on hardware: PLL4/PLL4_P/
ethck_k/ethrx all read back at the correct 750/125/125/125MHz with
or without this construct.

ST's own reference devicetree for this SoM family
(stm32mp15xx-dkx.dtsi, shared by DK1/DK2/EV1 and every official ST
evaluation kit) never had this construct in the first place - it was
added specifically for this board by the upstream contributor and,
as far as we can tell, never actually exercised against this driver
topology. Remove it to match how ST's own hardware does this.

Upstream-Status: Pending [should go upstream too - see rationale above]

--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/st/stm32mp157c-odyssey.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/st/stm32mp157c-odyssey.dts
@@ -37,9 +37,6 @@
 	phy-mode = "rgmii-id";
 	max-speed = <1000>;
 	phy-handle = <&phy0>;
-	assigned-clocks = <&rcc ETHCK_K>, <&rcc PLL4_P>;
-	assigned-clock-parents = <&rcc PLL4_P>;
-	assigned-clock-rates = <125000000>; /* Clock PLL4 to 750Mhz in ATF/U-Boot */
 	st,eth-clk-sel;

 	snps,reset-gpio = <&gpiog 0 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
